course: dictionary
lesson: 14498
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word peculiar is a good example. «The old man wore a peculiar hat with a feather and three buttons.» Here peculiar means strange or unusual, because the hat is odd to look at.
explain: Now read this: «Koalas are peculiar to Australia, and they live nowhere else in the wild.» Peculiar to means found only in one place, or belonging only to one thing. The words «live nowhere else» are the clue.
explain: Sometimes a character says, «I feel peculiar, and the room is spinning.» In British speech, feeling peculiar means feeling a bit ill or dizzy. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Peculiar means strange or unusual, sometimes in a slightly worrying way.
fact: «Peculiar to» means belonging only to one person, place or thing.
fact: In British informal speech, «feeling peculiar» means feeling a bit ill or dizzy.
fact: Peculiar is an adjective, and it can change to more peculiar and most peculiar.
fact: Look at the words around peculiar to find out which meaning the writer means.
exercise: «The shop sold a peculiar green cheese shaped like a star.» What does peculiar mean here? | *Strange and unusual | Sold out before lunch | Very heavy | Cheap and tasty
exercise: «Koalas are peculiar to Australia.» What does peculiar to mean here? | Very fast in Australia | *Found only in one place | Friendly to visitors from Australia | Always changing its name
exercise: Ella says, «I feel peculiar after the spinning ride.» What might she mean in British speech? | She has found a rare stamp | *She feels a bit ill or dizzy | She is going to a party | She feels very proud and happy
test: «Mum said the noise from the attic was peculiar, so we went up to look.» What does peculiar mean here? | Hot and dusty | *Strange and unusual | Very quiet and calm | Loud and cheerful
test: «The plant is peculiar to the rainforest, and it grows nowhere else.» Which words are the clue to the meaning? | the rainforest is big | is a plant | it is green | *grows nowhere else
exam: Which sentence uses peculiar with the meaning of belonging only to one place? | «I feel peculiar and sit down.» | *«The frog is peculiar to the islands.» | «The peculiar hat was red.» | «The peculiar noise woke the dog.»
